1. Use eic lAger data examples in https://eicweb.phy.anl.gov/monte_carlo/lager/-/tree/master/examples/eic?ref_type=heads to create the .json input files.
2. NB: the installation of lAger is here found https://eicweb.phy.anl.gov/monte_carlo/lager
3. Run ./bin/lager -c desire_directory_with_your_file/the_file.json -r 1 -o desire_directory_where_you_want _output 
4. Further examples of how to run your files are found here https://eicweb.phy.anl.gov/monte_carlo/lager
5. NB: DVMP study in our case requires running the afterburner on the hepmc from step 3 above with high acceptance (hi acc)
6. Following instructions on https://github.com/eic/afterburner


Data generated with lAger 3.6.1 - ./bin/lager -c desire_directory_with_your_file/the_file.json -r 1 -o desire_directory_where_you_want _output

Data passed through afterburner with preset ip6_ep_130x9 using abconv -p "ip6_ep_130x9" desire_directory_with_your_file/the_file.hepmc from the generator

Data converted to hepmc3.tree.root using - git clone https://github.com/eic/hepmc3ascii2root -> cmake -S . -B build -> ./build/hepmc3ascii2root input_file output_file done inside the eic-shell

Data is part of Exclusive_Diffractive_JPSI_ABCONV_9x130 dataset

The data ready for campaign production can be found : root://dtn-eic.jlab.org//work/eic3/users/Olaiya/9x130_GeV/

Further Info: Number of events: 19034 ;

Beam: 9x130 ;

Lum: 1fb-1 ;

Q2 range: 1<Q^2<10 ;

y range: 0.001<y<1

Total accepted cross section [nb]: 3.187455e-01 ;

Partial accepted cross section with BR [nb]: 1.903229e-02 ;

Acceptance [%]: 99.994747
